# Deliberately vulnerable-by-design A3 (SSH) fixture -- mixes legacy
# weak algorithms with modern/strong and PQC ones so a scan exercises
# every branch of protocol_scan.rs's ssh_algo_asset table.

# Weak: SHA-1-based group-1 key exchange.
KexAlgorithms diffie-hellman-group1-sha1,curve25519-sha256

# Weak: 3DES-CBC and RC4 (arcfour) ciphers alongside a strong AEAD one.
Ciphers 3des-cbc,arcfour,aes256-gcm@openssh.com,chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com

# Weak: plain HMAC-SHA1 alongside strong SHA-2 MACs.
MACs hmac-sha1,hmac-sha2-256,hmac-sha2-512

# Weak: ssh-rsa as a host-key algorithm (signature, quantum-vulnerable
# at the policy layer) alongside strong Ed25519/ECDSA.
HostKeyAlgorithms ssh-rsa,ssh-ed25519,ecdsa-sha2-nistp256

# Post-quantum hybrid key exchange (OpenSSH 10 default) -- Monitor
# tier, not quantum-vulnerable.
KexAlgorithms mlkem768x25519-sha256

